structure:
- 1 parent: sends cmd_status to child and waits for ackbyte from child. If received waits and receive data package from child 
- 3 children: 
    detects orientation through high signal at one of its 4 orientation pins (=start bit of CMD_STATUS) -> every communication between child and its parent now takes place through this orientation pin
    receives cmd_status from parent and sends ackByte to parent. 
    Afterwards it transitions into parent role (node) for its children -> transmits cmd_status to own children and waits for ack_busy -> Receives DATA FRAME from children (inlcuding SYNC, LEN, Payload, CRC) and saves information about connected children (child_mask) and
    combines it´s own data with the received data (SYNC, LEN (total), PAYLOAD (total), CRC) and sends them back to its own parent (upstream)
    => receive child frames, combine them with the node’s own data, and send one complete frame upstream.

PAYLOAD STRUCTURE
  NODE_ID ORIENTATION CHILD_MASK CHILD_PAYLOAD (=child frame without sync, len and crc)  

Sequence:
    1. idle: child waits for CMD_STATUS from parent on PA1
    1. idle: parent releases line
    2. parent: send CMD_STATUS -> reset
    3. parent: releases line

    4. Child/node scans upstream orientation pins.
    5. LOW detected on one upstream pin.
    6. Node receives CMD_STATUS on that pin.
    7. If byte != CMD_STATUS: discard event and return to idle.
    8. If byte == CMD_STATUS:
        active_upstream = detected pin
        orientation = detected pin index
    9. child/Node: sends ACK_BUSY upstream on active_upstream.
    10. Child/node polls own children with retries: (differences in v3, v2 and main)
        for each retry round:
            for each child i:
                if child already responded successfully:
                    skip
                send CMD_STATUS on child line i
                release child line i
                wait for ACK_BUSY
                if no ACK:
                    continue
                wait for DATA_FRAME
                validate child frame (CRC)
                store child frame
                set bit i in child_mask
    11. Child/Node builds own payload:
        NODE_ID
        ORIENTATION
        CHILD_MASK
        stored child payloads
    12. Child/Node sends own DATA_FRAME upstream:
        SYNC LEN PAYLOAD CRC

    13. Child/Node releases all lines and returns to idle.

    14. parent: receives DATA_FRAME
    15: Parent validates SYNC, LEN and CRC
    16: Parent compares payload with expected test payload

Pin assignment:
    PA1 = upstream data line (orientation 0)
    PA3 = upstream port 1 (orientation 1)
    PA4 = upstream port 2 (orientation 2)
    PA5 = upstream port 3 (orientation 3)
    PB0 = downstream child port 0
    PB1 = downstream child port 1
    PB4 = LED